WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.500
This is NextStep: a study planner for students juggling classes, work, and life.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:12.900
Meet Tobi. Tobi is fictional: a second-year student who works shifts at a print shop and rides the bus home.

3
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:23.467
Every day starts with Today: only what's realistic, the next session, and why it matters. Yesterday, three sessions didn't happen. That's okay.

4
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:30.067
When plans change, Tobi taps 'My plans changed', picks 'I have less time', and says forty-five minutes.

5
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:37.467
NextStep shows exactly what moves, with a reason for every change. Nothing changes until Tobi accepts.

6
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:51.733
Then there's one small next step. The focus timer is saved with timestamps, so it keeps counting even if the app closes.

7
00:00:56.867 --> 00:01:00.500
Afterwards, a quick check-in records what got done, and what's left.

8
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:08.133
Finishing it earns Back on Track: once, and only for real progress.

9
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:14.200
Progress builds along the journey, with a weekly rhythm instead of fragile daily streaks.

10
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:25.200
The week fits around work, lectures, and rest. Planning, Recovery Mode, and focus all work offline after setup, and sync when you reconnect.

11
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:30.600
NextStep. Plans change. Keep moving.
